# Practice-harvest / promote handoff state. The app writes snapshot.json into a
# member repo and agents write runs/<id>/result.json back; the ingest door then
# stamps ingested.json. All of it is machine-local ingest state, never source.
/practice-harvest/

# ts-rs default export dir. Bindings belong in src/lib/bindings/ (set via
# src-tauri/build.rs TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR); a cargo invocation that misses that env
# drops a duplicate tree here. Ignored so it never dirties the tree or drifts.
/bindings/

# .ai/ is tracked in full, data included (operator decision, 2026-08-28).
# The registry map, context index, consult log and lead outbox are all useful
# ACROSS DEVICES — the registry is consulted from more than one machine, and a
# lane that only exists on the box that generated it cannot be read by the next
# one. The known cost is accepted: registry-map.json is ~460 KB and is rewritten
# by /conform on every run, so it will churn in diffs. Verified before tracking:
# no absolute paths, usernames, emails or credentials in any of them (this
# repository is public).
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-28, because the rule this replaced asserted the opposite:
# the map does NOT churn every run. build-registry-map.mjs is deterministic —
# two consecutive runs with no code change differ by exactly one line, the
# `generatedAt` stamp. It moves when the repo or the registry actually moves
# (a 5-day-stale rebuild rewrote ~3k of 14.6k lines, all of it re-scored
# matches and newly governing subjects). That is signal, not noise.

